    {
      "id": "u_b79a58649e2c6100647db331_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "Trilium can automate this process. Select some text within the note, and in the selection toolbar, click the scissors icon for the \"cut & pasted selection to sub-note\" action. The heading is automatically detected and the new sub-note is named accordingly. You can also assign a keyboard shortcut for this action. This functionality is available through the block toolbar icon. On a phone, the scissors are at the end of the text formatting row, which shows as you select text.",
